  study and daily activities, decrease life quality, and bring about a heavy and hitherto unrecognized socioeconomic    
  burden."}, {"study_index": 7, "title": "Assessing the quality of reports of randomized clinical trials: is blinding   
  necessary?", "abstract": "It has been suggested that the quality of clinical trials should be assessed by blinded     
  raters to limit the risk of introducing bias into meta-analyses and systematic reviews, and into the peer-review      
  process. There is very little evidence in the literature to substantiate this. This study describes the development   
